{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Add an `mcp` autodeploy target to `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` implementing the ADR 0079\namendment's blue-green pointer-swap, so on-box `rebar-mcp` tracks `origin/main` without killing\nan in-flight certified op. Scope: the MCP deploy path only (service/edge = esok, secrets =\navians). No new timer: the existing `rebar-autodeploy.timer`→`.service` runs `autodeploy.sh`.\n\n## Approach (blue-green, ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur / 0079 amendment)\nModel on the LOCAL `origin/main` updater (`sticky-genetic-narwhal`): immutable release + atomic\npointer swap + retire-when-idle — NOT the review-bot stop-and-drain. On an MCP change:\n1. Build + tag immutable `compose-mcp:<target-sha>` (`docker compose build mcp`).\n2. **Memory pre-check BEFORE the 2x overlap** (t4g.large 8 GiB): read `MemAvailable` (`/proc/meminfo`,\n   MB); if a confident reading `< MCP_MEM_MIN_MB` (default 1024), ABORT — emit countable\n   `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT` marker (SNS-routed, see Alerting), record SHA-keyed backoff, start\n   NO second container (old keeps serving). Unreadable (non-Linux/absent) fails OPEN. Env override\n   `MCP_MEM_AVAILABLE_MB` makes it testable.\n3. Start a NEW container alongside old (one-in/one-out; never N) on the OTHER port of the A/B pair\n   (`MCP_PORT_A=8091`/`MCP_PORT_B=8092`, container port fixed 8091); current live port is read\n   back from the installed nginx include.\n4. Health-check the NEW `/health` 200 within `MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT` (default 120). On failure:\n   `docker rm -f` the new container, leave the OLD include UNCHANGED (rollback = do nothing),\n   emit `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` reason `mcp-unhealthy`, record backoff, exit 1 → next tick retries.\n5. **Atomically flip the nginx `/mcp/` upstream**: back up the installed include, write\n   `server 127.0.0.1:<newport>;` to a temp file and `mv` over `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf`\n   (atomic rename), `nginx -t`, then `nginx -s reload`. If `nginx -t`/reload fails: RESTORE the\n   backup (disk+loaded config agree on OLD), `docker rm -f` the new container, record backoff,\n   exit 1. Deploy is DONE at a successful reload; never waited on/killed an in-flight op.\n6. **Retire the OLD container off the critical path**, gated by a \"still serving?\" check on its\n   own `/health` `in_flight` gauge (long-running certified LLM ops only). Retain newest\n   `MCP_RELEASES_KEEP` (default 1) as rollback lifeline; remove older ones ONLY when idle\n   (`in_flight==0`); NEVER kill `in_flight>0`. If managed `rebar-mcp-*` count exceeds\n   `MCP_RELEASES_CAP` (default 3) because busy containers can't be reclaimed, emit countable\n   `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP` (SNS-routed) instead of killing a live one or growing unbounded.\n\nWhy: eliminates bug 7b4a (never-idle shared MCP can't satisfy a gauge-gated drain bound).\nDecoupling retire from deploy means the deploy never blocks or kills; a killed op is client-visible\n+ idempotent (event-sourced), so retire is safe.\n\n## Retire-when-idle re-trigger\n`autodeploy.sh` exits early when up-to-date, so a still-serving old container would only be\nrevisited on the next mcp change. Run a lightweight `mcp_retire_sweep` on the up-to-date/no-op\ntick (same placement as `reclaim_under_pressure`): reclaim idle old containers + fire the\nover-cap alert; no build/flip. So retirement re-triggers once the container goes idle.\n\n## Change detection + blast radius\n`MCP_PATHS='src/rebar infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp infra/compose/docker-compose.yml uv.lock pyproject.toml'`\n— the canonical set esok committed in the `mcp:` compose-comment contract this consumes. Diffed\n`deployed..target` it triggers ONLY `mcp`. Because `src/rebar` and `docker-compose.yml` are\nshared with `BOT_PATHS`, a shared change triggers BOTH targets, each in its own independent\n`if changed` block. `gerrit` is never touched (keep the existing gerrit-id assert; add a\nbefore/after gerrit-id assert across the mcp deploy too). `flock` still serializes.\n\n## Failure interaction with deployed-sha + backoff\nThe `mcp` branch failure is FATAL exactly like the `review-bot` branch: `record_backoff_failure`\n+ `exit 1`, so the footer that advances `deployed-sha` is not reached. For a shared change the\nreview-bot block runs first; if the review-bot succeeds but mcp fails, mcp records the backoff and\nexits 1, so `deployed-sha` does not advance and BOTH retry next tick (review-bot rebuild is\nidempotent). A failed mcp deploy is therefore always retried.\n\n## Alerting (marker → observability → CloudWatch → SNS; NO direct SNS publish)\nautodeploy.sh has no `sns:Publish` path and must not gain one. The alert is emitted like every\nexisting autodeploy alert: a countable `marker AUTODEPLOY_MCP_* {json}` → `observability.sh`\ngreps the unit journal via `publish_autodeploy_marker_delta` into a dimensionless `rebar/host`\nmetric → a terraform `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm` routes it to `aws_sns_topic.alerts.arn`\n(`rebar-gerrit-alerts`). This ticket adds: tokens `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP` +\n`AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT`; two `publish_autodeploy_marker_delta` calls (+ offset files) in\nobservability.sh publishing `rebar/host:mcp_retire_cap` + `rebar/host:mcp_mem_abort`; two\n`aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm` resources mirroring `monitoring_autodeploy.tf`'s dimensionless\n900s/2-of-4/Sum>0/notBreaching shape. Both tokens are distinct from `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` (so they\ndon't inflate deploy_errors) and are redacted from any captured container output.\n\n## Portability (`project.portability`)\nTrigger is the existing on-box systemd/launchd-style timer polling the git mirror — an\noperation-linked poll, not a CI provider. Drain/flip/retire run in-process; works with any/no CI.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tier: **real subprocess/bash integration, temp git repos + fake docker/nginx** (§3\n  CLI/env/exit codes + git refs). Tests stub the box binaries onto PATH and run the REAL\n  `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`, in `tests/scripts/` beside the sibling autodeploy tests. Oracles:\n  - Change detection (REAL temp git repo, two commits): an MCP-only change (touch\n    `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp`) triggers `mcp` and NO review-bot/gerrit rebuild; a\n    review-bot-only change (touch `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot`, not in `MCP_PATHS`) does\n    the inverse; a shared `src/rebar` change triggers BOTH independently — via the docker call log.\n  - Cutover order start-new → health → flip → retire (recorded docker/nginx/curl call log) and the\n    deploy returns success WITHOUT waiting on `in_flight` (with `in_flight>0` on OLD it still flips\n    the include to the new port and exits 0).\n  - Retire honors liveness: an OLD container with `in_flight>0` is NOT killed (no `docker rm` of\n    it); over `MCP_RELEASES_CAP` the `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP` marker is emitted and no live\n    container is deleted.\n  - Memory pre-check: `MCP_MEM_AVAILABLE_MB < MCP_MEM_MIN_MB` ABORTS the overlap — no second\n    container started, `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT` marker emitted, backoff recorded, old include\n    unchanged.\n  - Health-check failure on the new container leaves the OLD include UNCHANGED (rollback: include\n    byte-identical, `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` reason `mcp-unhealthy`, backoff recorded, `deployed-sha`\n    not advanced); a retry on the next healthy tick flips the include (§5D).\n  - `gerrit` container id UNCHANGED across an mcp deploy (blast-radius oracle).\n- [ ] observability.sh publishes `rebar/host:mcp_retire_cap` + `rebar/host:mcp_mem_abort` from the\n  two markers (asserted via the sibling observability marker-publish test pattern).\n- [ ] Two terraform CloudWatch alarms route the two metrics to `aws_sns_topic.alerts.arn`,\n  mirroring `monitoring_autodeploy.tf`.\n\n## Compat / rollback\nAdditive (new independent `if changed \"$MCP_PATHS\"` block + no-op sweep); other targets\nunchanged (existing autodeploy tests stay green). ADRs 0079/0104 document it. Rollback = revert\nthe mcp branch + observability/terraform additions.\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur (ADR), cibophobic-holohedral-esok (upstream + `/health`)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787624027325431001,"uuid":"d8a0b4c3-a65e-445e-abd1-3315be22d09f"}